{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/992756-ghoul-merit","id":992756,"title":"Ghoul merit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-24T21:27:56-07:00","id":992756,"title":"Ghoul merit","content":"Not sure whether to put this here, in general, or in Hunter, since it's meant primarily for the latter two, but I'm wondering if anyone has tried to write up ghoulhood as a merit. I was specifically thinking of ghoul hunters, and I feel like having it as a (entirely optional and ST-approval required) merit could be a cool way to handle that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T22:15:37-07:00","id":992780,"title":"","content":"While not a Merit, I had a Hunter <i>ages</i> ago that never saw play who used some combination of rules to get a handful of Dread Powers. I think there's a Merit that lets you do that?<br /> <br /> But anyway, he was a Cheiron employee named Ridley Duquette who had one of their teams to thank for killing his regnant, and now brings in vampires for the company in exchange for monthly doses of vampiric blood. It's a win-win!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T22:27:09-07:00","id":992781,"title":"","content":"That's a really cool concept! But I'm going for the easiest possible solution for ghouls in a mortals or Hunter chronicle. <br /> <br /> So, what about dot cost? Four? Five? It's a pretty big thing, but it has some major drawbacks, so I don't really see it being that overpowered. Do we have Dread Powers be part of the merit, or do we have the merit include a system for buying them?<br /> <br /> We should probably wait to see how 2e does Dread Powers (presumably using some refinement of the Blue Book rules). I forget, are there different ranks of Dread Powers? We'd need some mechanism to restrict Ghouls to only lower-level powers. I'd have to reread the ghoul section, too. I'd imagine some resistance to diseases and poisons, maybe even to zombie plagues and such, but something like an Ascending Ones superpoison or a plague-spirit on the rampage could probably poison them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T23:22:59-07:00","id":992803,"title":"","content":"What benefit is there in it being a merit you have to spend xp towards compared to a less template you can get for free? There's no reason a hunter couldn't be a ghoul already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T23:34:00-07:00","id":992807,"title":"","content":"Honestly, it all comes down to design preference. I would prefer there it to exist as a merit, to keep things as simple as possible. There is no reason (other than many potential plot considerations) why a hunter couldn't be a ghoul, but making it a merit makes handling it simpler and raises it more evidently as a possibility. <br /> <br /> Hm, if I'm remembering correctly, didn't Ascension have ghouldom as a merit?<br /> <br /> And once we finally get Half-Damned, we could work out a dhampir merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T00:00:32-07:00","id":992828,"title":"","content":"Look at the ghoul rules, compress those into 1-3 paragraphs, and you have ghouls as a merit. It's more paperwork because you have to compress it instead of just giving them the template for free, but if you want it as a merit, that'd be how you'd do it. <br /> <br /> They get Vitae = to Stamina. Lose one a month. Get 1-2 discipline dots, can heal by spending vitae, drawback: you're probably blood-bonded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T00:12:29-07:00","id":992834,"title":"","content":"That sounds good, with one minor thing. The problem with Discipline dots is that it means you need to bring the Discipline system into Hunter, and I'm looking for a way to convert that to Dread Powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T00:19:27-07:00","id":992835,"title":"","content":"If you're bringing Ghouls over from Requiem, why not just use the Disciplines? With Ghouls you already need things like a Vitae pool, the conditions that come with the Blood Bond etc. so its not like there aren't already reasons you'll need access to the Requiem book if you want to make this a thing in Hunter. I'd also personally say that keeping the Disciplines would add a more unique flavour to the Ghouled hunter. Hunter players are used to seeing the Dread Powers, so Disciplines would hopefully be more of a surprise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T00:27:53-07:00","id":992838,"title":"","content":"Basically, the thing is, the dread powers system allows Hunter to use vampires without having to use the Requiem book. I'm trying to do something similar with ghouls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T01:24:20-07:00","id":992846,"title":"","content":"Just give them access to the vampiric dread powers from Night Stalkers at lower level. Thats the hunter equivalent to disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/422-lykas","name":"Lykas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar422_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T01:27:31-07:00","id":992848,"title":"","content":"I had something like that planned, but how do we fold that into a merit? Presumably the ghoul doesn't get access to all of them from one merit. Maybe the merit can be purchased multiple times, each time including another Dread Power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T01:36:07-07:00","id":992850,"title":"","content":"Make a merit, that restrict a ghoul to take too mich dread powers. Somthing linke:<br /> Ghoul (1-5)<br /> The Charakter gains acces to vampiric dread powers. He just can buy a total sum of (fitting Attribute)+Ghoul Merit oft points in these dread powers.<br /> <br /> So he has potential to grow but he isn't so powerful as a real Vampire.<br /> <br /> (Sry my mobilephone wants to correct in german ^^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/422-lykas","name":"Lykas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar422_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T08:21:56-07:00","id":994595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/992756-ghoul-merit?p=992848#post992848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had something like that planned, but how do we fold that into a merit? Presumably the ghoul doesn't get access to all of them from one merit. Maybe the merit can be purchased multiple times, each time including another Dread Power?</div> </div> </div> </div>How's this?<br /> <br /> <b>Ghoul (\u25cf - \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</b><br /> You have been tainted by the blood of Vampires. While this has left you dependent on that blood, you also benefit from a measure of their powers.<br /> <b>Benefit:</b> You can buy Dread Powers rated at one or two dots as Merits of an equivalent rating. You are not limited in how many distinct Dread Powers you can acquire, but see &quot;Drawback&quot; below.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> You require a monthly dose of fresh Vampire blood to live. You need to ingest or inject Vampire blood equivalent to 1 Lethal damage for the Vampire each month, fresh from the source (you cannot store it for longer than a day), +1 Lethal damage per dot of Dread Powers beyond your rating in this merit. If you fail to feed in a given month, you suffer 1 Lethal damage per day until you feed.<br /> <br /> It gives you access to Dread Powers, but it caps it so you aren't getting the really strong ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T12:18:43-07:00","id":994742,"title":"","content":"That pretty much covers what I was looking for, thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}